# 📈 Finance & Stock Analytics — End-to-End Portfolio Project

> **Tools:** Python · MySQL · Tableau &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Level:** Junior / Entry-level  
> **Dataset:** 10 fictional stocks · 10,430 daily price rows · 160 quarterly earnings records · 2021–2024

---

## What This Project Demonstrates

This project walks through a complete data analytics workflow applied to stock market and corporate revenue data. It's designed to show the kind of work a junior data analyst would be expected to do: clean data, write SQL, explore patterns in Python, build a simple model, and communicate findings visually.

**Three questions drive the analysis:**

1. *Which stocks and sectors performed best — and when did the market struggle?*
2. *How do companies compare on revenue growth and profitability?*
3. *Can we predict next month's stock return from historical patterns?*

---

## Project Structure

```
finance_analytics/
│
├── data/                          ← All generated CSV files live here
│   ├── stock_prices.csv           # Daily OHLCV for 10 fictional tickers
