## Charts Generated

| # | Chart | Key Insight |
|---|-------|-------------|
| 01 | Indexed Stock Performance | All stocks normalised to 100 — easy comparison |
| 02 | Annual Returns Heatmap | Year × ticker grid, colour = return |
| 03 | Rolling Volatility | 20-day annualised vol for 3 selected stocks |
| 04 | Return Distributions | Histogram + normal fit per stock |
| 05 | Quarterly Revenue (Stacked) | Sector contribution over time |
| 06 | Margin vs Revenue Scatter | Bubble size = market cap |
| 07 | Correlation Matrix | Which stocks move together? |
| 08 | Actual vs Predicted Returns | Model performance (test set) |
| 09 | Feature Coefficients | What drives the model's predictions? |
| 10 | Residual Analysis | Is the model well-behaved? |

---

## SQL Queries Overview

| # | Query | Technique Used |
|---|-------|----------------|
| Q1 | Annual return per stock | `FIRST_VALUE`, `LAST_VALUE`, `RANK()` |
| Q2 | Month-over-month price change | `LAG()` window function |
| Q3 | 20-day & 50-day moving average | `ROWS BETWEEN` frame clause |
| Q4 | Sector performance + Sharpe proxy | `STDDEV`, aggregation, CTEs |
| Q5 | Revenue YoY growth per quarter | `LAG()` across years |
| Q6 | Top 3 revenue quarters per company | `RANK()` with partition |
| Q7 | Avg profit margin by sector & year | `GROUP BY` aggregation |
| Q8 | Volatility risk bucketing | `CASE WHEN` bucketing |
| Q9 | 52-week high and low | `MAX`, `MIN` with date filter |
| Q10 | Full portfolio dashboard summary | Multi-CTE, multi-join |

---

## About the Prediction Model

The Ridge Regression model predicts next month's stock return using:
- Last 3 months of lagged returns (momentum signal)
- Recent volatility
- Sector dummy variables

**The R² on the 2024 test set is low — and that's intentional and correct to report.**

*Built with Python 3.12 · MySQL 8.0 · Tableau Public*  
*Dataset: fully synthetic, no real market data used*

